Body:
@Crazyphil 
Thank you so much, but there are a tad bugs in the instruction you provided:
1. `opencode.jsonc` missed one `}` at the end (probably copy-paste issue). Correct version:
```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "mistral-openai": {
      "name": "Mistral (OpenAI)",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "models": {
        "zai-glm-5-2": {
          "name": "GLM-5.2",
          "attachment": true,
          "reasoning": true,
          "temperature": true,
          "tool_call": true,
          "limit": {
            "context": 1000000,
            "output": 131072
          },
          "modalities": {
            "input": [
              "text"
            ],
            "output": [
              "text"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.mistral.ai/v1"
      }
    }
  }
}
```
2. I don't know if it's just me, but [mistral-glm-model.js](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31229323/mistral-glm-model.js) will cause build error.  
   I changed its extension to .ts then it works.
   I.e. grab `mistral-glm-model.js` and rename it as `mistral-glm-model.ts`

Anyway, thank you for the workaround since opencode feels much better than Mistral's official cli tool.

I can confirm that this behavior also occurs in the interactive TUI with opencode2 v0.0.0-beta-18050.

I have different models configured for the primary agents:

```
{
  "agents": {
    "plan": {
      "model": "openai/gpt-5.6-terra"
    },
    "build": {
      "model": "opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash"
    }
  }
}
```

opencode2 debug agents resolves all 2 agents and their models correctly.

However, when switching between plan and build in the interactive TUI, the selected agent changes but the configured model does not change with it.
